# OpenWolf bug memory is an append-only JSON Lines log: one JSON object per
# line, no shared closing bracket and no trailing comma to fight over. `union`
# is a git built-in, so every clone and worktree resolves concurrent appends
# from parallel branches automatically with no local `git config` step. A single
# shared JSON array could not do this: a union merge of that shape drops the
# comma between the two branches' last entries and yields invalid JSON.
#
# Union merge keeps both sides' lines. Entries are therefore never rewritten in
# place; see the store contract in .wolf/hooks/shared.js.
.wolf/buglog.jsonl merge=union
